[pete@titan.rice.edu (Pete Keleher) wonders:]
[]Does anybody have more information on this alignment business. I'd really
[]like to be able to turn potions of water into holy water even with chaotic
[]alignment, is this possible? Are the holy water business and which kind of
[]alter that you can sacrifice at the only differences between alignments?

you can change your intrinsic alignment but this is fraught with peril
and not recommended.

you can wear a different hat! and in the process you may change your
alignment. this is effortless and carries no penalties.

generally, altars can be converted to your current alignment by sacrificing
at them. given this fact and the previous one(s), you can effectively create
lawful altars in any game. however that isn't necessary if you can find
and identify just one potion of holy water. with that one potion you can
create as much holy water as you desire ...

different monsters have different alignments which can affect how they
react to you. as an example, golden nagas and titans (curse casting
monsters) are lawful and typically won't attack a lawful character.

the gifts the gods may give you are divided along alignment lines.

